Firmware: ODROID-C5 bootloader: Amlogic's boot stages (BL2 and the stages it loads,
          BL30, BL31 and BL32, with their signed headers) and Hardkernel's U-Boot (BL33)
Hardware: Hardkernel ODROID-C5 (Amlogic S905X5M, SoC family S7D)
Files:    the SD card's bootloader area: the MBR's boot code and the sectors from 1
          up to the first partition (at most 8 MiB); this file on the SD card's boot
          partition as /BOOTLOADER.txt
Source:   This notice is for a card made with ODROID_C5_BOOTLOADER_FROM; a card
          made with the firmware package amlogic-s7d-bootloader carries that
          package's notice instead.  Here the area is not fetched by zedBSD: it
          is copied, byte for byte, from the card
          image named by ODROID_C5_BOOTLOADER_FROM, which is expected to be one of
          Hardkernel's own ODROID-C5 operating system images, obtained by whoever
          builds the image.  The lines after "Copied from" on the card's copy name
          that image and the SHA-256 of the area taken from it.
          Hardkernel's build tree for this bootloader is the branch
          odroidc5-v2023.01 of https://github.com/hardkernel/u-boot (at
          c99f3409d5cad031b365fd871e543f97af893f88, "ODROID-C5: Firmware update
          with Amlogic BSP 202508"); the Amlogic stages and the U-Boot source are
          its submodules on git.odroid.com.
          A donor known to work with this notice: the signed bootloader of
          Hardkernel's Yocto layer for the ODROID-C5,
          https://github.com/mdrjr/meta-odroid-aml at commit
          548e2f037e01c626e3fc964fa298464df148fd51, file
          recipes-bsp/u-boot-odroid-c5/files/u-boot.bin.signed (3379200 bytes,
          SHA-256 8c2e66919a05921d79e130cc00a977a07cf8df6b34153e66c18c3241c0809e3c;
          its BL30 names the SoC "S7D-s905x5m"), placed from sector 1 as that
          layer's odroid-c5.wks does (rawcopy, --offset 1S); the donor file is
          512 zero bytes followed by it, so the MBR's boot code stays zero.

Copyright Amlogic, Inc. (the boot stages BL2 to BL32)
Copyright the U-Boot authors and Hardkernel Co., Ltd. (U-Boot)

Terms:
- U-Boot is GPL-2.0-or-later.  Its corresponding source is Hardkernel's: the
  submodule bl33/v2023 of the branch above (https://git.odroid.com/yocto/uboot,
  branch odroidc5-v2023.01).  zedBSD changes nothing in it.
- Amlogic's boot stages are binaries Amlogic gives to board makers.  No licence
  text for them was found in Hardkernel's public tree or image, nor in the
  Yocto layer above (its recipe states GPL-2.0-only, for U-Boot only), and no
  public download of them alone was found.  Their redistribution terms are therefore
  unknown: an SD card image made with ODROID_C5_BOOTLOADER_FROM carries
  Amlogic's binaries as Hardkernel ships them, is for the use of whoever built
  it with their own copy of Hardkernel's image, and is not to be passed on
  until the terms are known.  A card image made with ODROID_C5_NO_BOOTLOADER=y
  carries none of them.
- The boot ROM accepts only stages signed for the S905X5M, so the area is used
  as it is; zedBSD does not modify, re-sign or rebuild it.
